<figure class="horizon" aria-labelledby="r32-horizon-title">
 <figcaption id="r32-horizon-title"><span>Figure 1</span> Vacuum cannot move past the report’s need</figcaption>
 <div class="history">
 <div><b>1 · Report takes snapshot</b><div class="version">P7 · 20.00<span>visible to report</span></div><p>The report remains open.</p></div>
 <div><b>2 · Writer commits 25.00</b><div class="version">P7 · 20.00<span>still needed by report</span></div><div class="version new">P7 · 25.00<span>visible to fresh reader</span></div><p>Vacuum keeps both tuple bodies.</p></div>
 <div><b>3 · Report ends; vacuum runs</b><div class="version empty">Reusable space<span>old tuple removed</span></div><div class="version new">P7 · 25.00<span>visible to all snapshots</span></div><p>The page can become all-visible.</p></div>
 </div>
 <p class="caption">A conceptual schedule matching the native check below. The cleanup boundary is about snapshots that can still need versions, rather than a fixed number of seconds after commit. The last vacuum also requested freezing; an all-visible page is not automatically all-frozen.</p>
</figure>
